title ALES38 — Lotus's seal, made general: one verify-before-trust law both sheets call
prompt Continue the ALES recursion loop Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds and make progress before checking in; send each finished increment to origin and xykj61 as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur
think ALES37's own road-on named two next rungs: a session file bundling rack + cue over one master, or the refactor that lifts the shared seal into one place both wrappers call. Read rack_seal.rye and cue_seal.rye side by side — they duplicate the whole verify-before-trust frame verbatim: to_hex, the digest_prefix / 64-hex-width constants, the entire seal_* body-render-and-backfill, and the entire verify_and_parse header/digest-line location + Sha256 compare. They differ only in the sealed_header string and which parser consumes the verified body (rack_sheet.parse_rack vs cue_sheet.parse_sheet, the latter also taking a master).
think Chose the refactor as the crux, Lindy-first crux-first. Lindy: a named reused primitive is read thousands of times; two copies of one law is a drift waiting to happen. Crux-first: this is the decisive move that opens the coming session file cleanly — a session file seals a COMPOSITE body (rack sheet + cue sheet), and a general primitive serves it zero-scratch rather than entrenching a third hand-rolled seal. Doing it now, while only two callers exist, is the cheapest the consolidation will ever be. And ALES37's reading already made the discovery ("the seal is a law for any travels-as-text record") — this makes that discovery real in code.
think Shape: lotus/seal.rye, a pure primitive over std.crypto only (no audio imports). Three functions carry it PARSER-AGNOSTIC. begin(out, header) writes the header line + digest prefix, reserves exactly 64 hex + newline, returns a Frame{hex_at, body_at}. The caller renders its body directly into out[body_at..] (one sheet, or a composite). finish(out, frame, body_len) hashes exactly those bytes and backfills the digest — zero scratch, infallible (begin already proved the fit). open(text, header) is the integrity gate before trust: locate header + digest line, recompute Sha256, return the body SLICE only on a match. The generalization is exact because open returns BYTES not a parsed structure, so the one honest per-format difference (cue_sheet.parse_sheet bounds positions against a master) lives in the caller after the gate.
think Refactored rack_seal.rye and cue_seal.rye onto it — each keeps its own distinct sealed_header and its own error set (RackSealError = seal.SealError || rack_sheet.RackSheetError; CueSealError = seal.SealError || cue_sheet.MarkerTextError; Zig merges error sets by name so BadRecord/Overflow coincide rather than double). seal_* became begin -> render body in place -> finish; verify_and_parse became const body = try seal.open(text, sealed_header); try <parser>(body, ...). The rendered bytes are byte-for-byte unchanged, so the refactor is proven by both shipped witnesses staying GREEN — not merely by the new one.
obs GREEN across the board. seal.rye selftest GREEN on the first build (six cases: an arbitrary body round-trips whole through begin/finish/open; a wrong header, a missing / short / non-hex digest line each refuse BadRecord; a flipped body byte and a truncated tail each refuse DigestMismatch; a too-small buffer refuses Overflow). Both shipped seal witnesses (ales_rack_seal, ales_cue_seal) stayed GREEN after the refactor — the byte-for-byte proof of the generalization. Downstream ales_rack_merge (which composes rack_seal.verify_and_parse) GREEN. tame_style_check GREEN (bans clean); width-check clean.
obs Migrated the one new @memcpy the selftest wanted to tally_copy.copy_disjoint (added lotus/tally_copy.rye -> ../tally/copy.rye symlink, matching linengrow's convention) so no new @memcpy application site enters the tree. Purely local — a Sha256 over an in-process text record; no socket, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device, no real meter, no real speaker; every custody gate untouched.
loom witness=ales_seal_witness result=green digest=sha256 hex_len=64 build=first cases=6 refactored=rack_seal+cue_seal both_green=true downstream=ales_rack_merge_green
file lotus/seal.rye ALES38 module — begin / finish / open, the verify-before-trust seal lifted to one parser-agnostic primitive over std.crypto only
file lotus/rack_seal.rye refactored onto seal.rye — seal_rack via begin/finish, verify_and_parse via seal.open; witness stays GREEN byte-for-byte
file lotus/cue_seal.rye refactored onto seal.rye — seal_sheet via begin/finish, verify_and_parse via seal.open with the master passthrough after the gate
file lotus/tally_copy.rye symlink to ../tally/copy.rye so the selftest copies via copy_disjoint, no new @memcpy site
file tools/ales_seal_witness.rish the witness that builds and proves seal.rye GREEN on metal
file active-designing/20260814-153840_fill-ales38-lotus-seal.md the self-approved design read for the round
file lotus/README.md front door synced — status list (ALES38 seal generalized), the seal.rye rung entry, road-on paragraph, stamp
recommend keep-going ALES39 the session file is now clean composition — begin, render the rack sheet and the cue sheet into one body over one master, finish, and a single seal.open verifies the whole project before any of it is trusted; the SIGNED carry (Kumara key) and the ALES0-wire carry stay module seams for Keaton's word
